<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/><title>BlackRock Tracker | Matrix Reprogrammed</title><meta name="description" content="Big Three asset manager tracker: BlackRock, Vanguard and State Street."/><link rel="stylesheet" href="../styles.css"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="../reader-experience.css"/><style id="public-internal-visibility">.internal-only,[data-internal-only="true"]{display:none!important}</style></head><body><canvas id="matrix"></canvas><div class="signal-face"></div><div class="veil"></div><div class="page"><header class="wrap topbar"><a class="brand" href="../index.html"><img src="../sigil.png" alt="Matrix Reprogrammed sigil"/> MATRIX REPROGRAMMED</a><nav class="nav"><a href="../big-three-asset-managers.html">Big Three</a><a href="../elite-reports.html">Reports</a><a href="../entities.html">Entities</a><a href="../evidence-vault.html">Evidence</a><a href="../search.html">Search</a></nav></header><!-- page-guide:start --><section class="page-guide wrap"><div><span class="label">You are here</span><h2>Site route</h2><p>This page is part of the wider reporting system. Start with the summary, then open the evidence route or research tools for deeper source work.</p></div><div class="page-guide-chips"><span>Summary</span><span>Evidence</span><span>Research</span><span>Search</span></div><div class="page-guide-actions"><a class="btn" href="../daily-command-brief.html">Today</a><a class="btn alt" href="../evidence-vault.html">Evidence</a><a class="btn alt" href="../research-tools.html">Research Tools</a></div></section><!-- page-guide:end --><!-- reader-governor:start --><section class="reader-governor-strip"><div><strong>Matrix Reprogrammed</strong><span>Reports, records, people, institutions, money routes and missing files.</span></div><nav><a href="../daily-command-brief.html">Daily Brief</a><a href="../control-structure.html">Power Map</a><a href="../entities.html">Entities</a><a href="../investigations.html">Investigations</a><a href="../evidence-vault.html">Evidence</a><a href="../search.html">Search</a></nav></section><!-- reader-governor:end --><main><section class="hero wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Big Three Profile</div><h1>BLACKROCK</h1><p class="lead">Latest public watch: about $13.46T reported for Q3 2025; verify against latest 10-Q/earnings release before quoting.</p><div class="cta-row"><a class="btn" href="../big-three-asset-managers.html">Big Three Hub</a><a class="btn alt internal-only" href="../data/big-three-asset-managers.json">Machine Data</a><a class="btn alt" href="../evidence-vault.html">Evidence Vault</a></div></section><section class="section wrap"><div class="grid"><article class="card redline"><h2>Management / board</h2><ul><li>Laurence D. Fink — chairman and CEO watch route</li><li>Robert S. Kapito — president watch route</li><li>Board, executive committee, risk committee and stewardship leadership to be refreshed from annual report / proxy statement</li></ul></article><article class="card"><h2>Control layers</h2><ul><li>index funds and ETFs</li><li>iShares</li><li>Aladdin risk and portfolio platform</li><li>private markets / infrastructure expansion</li><li>proxy voting / stewardship</li><li>public-company ownership concentration</li></ul></article><article class="card redline"><h2>Contracts / mandates to track</h2><ul><li>USASpending.gov entity search</li><li>SAM.gov entity search</li><li>SEC material agreements and acquisition filings</li><li>public pension and state investment board mandates</li><li>sovereign wealth / institutional mandate references</li></ul></article><article class="card"><h2>Source routes</h2><ul><li>BlackRock investor relations</li><li>BlackRock annual report / 10-K</li><li>SEC EDGAR company filings</li><li>SEC 13F filings</li><li>Form ADV adviser search</li><li>N-PX proxy voting records</li><li>USASpending.gov</li><li>OpenSecrets lobbying search</li></ul></article><article class="card redline"><h2>Watch triggers</h2><ul><li>AUM movement</li><li>ETF flows</li><li>top 13F holdings</li><li>proxy voting themes</li><li>public pension mandates</li><li>government or central-bank-adjacent work</li><li>Aladdin / technology partnerships</li><li>acquisitions and private-market expansion</li><li>regulatory actions and lawsuits</li></ul></article><article class="card"><h2>Missing records</h2><ul><li>latest official AUM table</li><li>current executive committee list</li><li>latest 13F parsed holdings</li><li>latest proxy voting dataset</li><li>government contract extract</li><li>public pension mandate list</li><li>lobbying spend summary</li></ul></article><article class="card"><h2>What cannot be concluded</h2><p>Asset ownership, index exposure, custody, fund voting, platform use or public contract appearance is not proof of wrongdoing by itself. Upgrade only with records.</p></article></div></section><section id="blackrock-video-claim-audit" class="section wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Uploaded Video Research</div><h2>BlackRock Viral Claim Audit</h2><p class="lead">The uploaded videos are now treated as source leads: one shows repeated asset-manager holder screenshots and Bank of America / Giannini history; the other frames families, orders and policy groups as a control structure. This page separates visible claims, public-record routes and unsupported speculation.</p><div class="grid"><article class="card redline"><h3>What the screenshots really show</h3><ul><li>Do not read the screenshots as “BlackRock owns everything.” Read them as “index money causes the same asset managers to appear across many companies.”</li><li>The real power question is not just share ownership. It is voting rights, proxy policy, fund mandates, pension mandates, stewardship, Aladdin technology, private-market expansion and government-adjacent work.</li><li>The strongest BlackRock brief should ask: who owns the shares, who votes them, who sets the policy, who benefits from the mandate, and what record proves it?</li></ul></article><article class="card"><h3>What public records can verify</h3><ul><li>BlackRock is one of the world’s largest asset managers and reported roughly $11.6T AUM at the end of 2024; later reports place it higher, so every quoted figure needs date/version control.</li><li>BlackRock often appears as a top holder because funds and ETFs hold shares on behalf of clients. The key distinction is beneficial ownership versus voting/stewardship influence.</li><li>BlackRock, Vanguard and State Street create common-ownership concentration across many listed companies. This is a serious structural question even when no wrongdoing is alleged.</li><li>A. P. Giannini founded the Bank of Italy, which became Bank of America. The 1906 earthquake story is a banking-history route, not proof of a BlackRock control chain.</li><li>The most important evidence routes are 13F holdings, 13D/13G beneficial ownership, N-PX proxy votes, Form ADV, annual reports, litigation, lobbying and public mandate records.</li></ul></article><article class="card redline"><h3>Evidence routes to pull next</h3><ul><li>BlackRock annual reports and investor relations</li><li>SEC EDGAR: 10-K, 10-Q, 13F, 13D/13G, 8-K</li><li>N-PX proxy voting records</li><li>Form ADV adviser records</li><li>Reuters / major finance reporting for date-specific AUM snapshots</li><li>Bank of America historical material on A. P. Giannini</li><li>public pension and procurement databases</li></ul></article><article class="card"><h3>Watch next</h3><ul><li>Parse latest BLK 10-K and 10-Q for AUM, risk factors, acquisitions and client mix.</li><li>Parse latest BlackRock 13F and compare top holdings against Vanguard and State Street.</li><li>Build N-PX voting summary: how often BlackRock votes with management, against management and on climate/social/governance proposals.</li><li>Add public mandate table for pensions, sovereign institutions, state funds and central-bank-adjacent work where records exist.</li><li>Separate viral claims into proven, partly supported, unproven and false/misleading buckets.</li></ul></article><article class="card redline"><h3>Boundary</h3><p>Uploaded videos are treated as leads. Claims are upgraded only through filings, official records, court records, annual reports, ownership data and proxy-voting records.</p><a class="btn internal-only" href="../data/blackrock-video-claim-audit.json">Open Machine Audit</a></article></div></section></main><footer class="footer wrap"><p><strong>Boundary:</strong> this page maps public-record influence routes and missing records. It does not treat ownership or fund exposure as wrongdoing.</p></footer></div><script src="../matrix.js"></script><script type="application/json" id="public-copy-internal-vault" data-internal-only="true">{"purpose":"Internal routes, commercial strategy and operational labels retained for audits but hidden from normal public navigation.","hiddenRoutes":["review-dashboard.html","deploy-status.html","deploy-health.html","card-system-health.html","site-brain-router.html","card-artwork-automation.html","card-artwork-queue.html","conclusion-engine.html","information-gathering-system.html","source-intake.html","update-monitor.html","distribution-center.html","launch-room.html","offer-center.html","sales-ladder.html","schema-index.html","machine-index.html","campaign-calendar.html","card-art-studio.html"],"labels":["Sell / Capture","Site Brain Router","Money Engine","Reader Money Path","Matrix Reprogrammed Status","Mission + Money Engine","Capture System","Monetisation Dashboard"]}</script></body></html>